  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nThis frozen T37 whole-owner construction raises the conditional bound from PR #890's **0.001661957774647029** to **0.001661960547713947**, an absolute gain of **0.000000002773066918**. The gain is tiny; the U8 local word and PR589 bit supplier are unchanged.\n\nThe witness combines T21 and T16 call orders and applies eight whole-role edits. It admits 167,832 roles across 333 complete calls, with idle profile `{48:11086, 1:6}`. The package includes an independent reconstruction, literal owner/window/chart checks, emitted-controller admission, exact arithmetic receipts, and a supporting signed-dual inequality that gives the same `10^-18` grid upper bound for every positive replica count in this fixed U8/width/capacity/outer-recipe family.\n\n**Changed hypothesis:** the conservative complex prefix is 779 bits, exceeding PR890's 512-bit allowance. This construction explicitly charges 1024 bits and recomputes its row charge and finite bootstrap cutoffs. The resulting row coefficient is `17495 < 20161`; the bit supplier retains its original 512-bit charge. The all-T arithmetic relaxation alone does not establish physical admission.\n\nThe first commit copies 64 prerequisite files from PR #890 head `4b3bd8cbe8e3e81c44161017c9b72c905a8040a8` byte-for-byte, preserving its manifests and attribution. The second commit contains the new T37 package and focused CI. The repository's selected result and upstream sources are unchanged.\n\nAll-size/compiler, common-label and physical realization, whole-call hosting, precision/tape, analytic transfer and bit H1-H5 remain inherited assumptions. This is a finite conditional construction, not an unconditional theorem or a full historical-suite audit. Source credit and substantial OpenAI Codex assistance are disclosed in `research/complex-t37-owners/NOTICE.md`; no independent human review is claimed.\n\n## Validation\n\nPassed locally on the committed package:\n\n- Complete cold PR589/PR741/PR799 predecessor rebuild: all six top-level stages succeeded, including the fixed 22-stage PR741 coverage.\n- Fresh U8/T37 replay against that new baseline: all 13 stages succeeded; final binding confirms the source manifest remained identical throughout. The strict result is `0.001661960547713947`.\n- 14 package-boundary/optimized-mode checks; 12 actual-file binding mutations and eight optimized-run rejections. The successful replay and source files remained unchanged during mutation tests.\n- Both exact moment engines, adjacent-grid rejection, all 47 strict outer inequalities, full owner/window/chart recount, partial-bank checks, strict prefix/row boundaries, and inherited controller/assembly/bit control inventories.\n- Linux/Python 3.12 full replay; Windows/Python 3.14 package controls and independent all-T arithmetic. Working tree clean and staged/committed bytes match the source pins.\n\nReproduction from the repository root (new output paths outside the checkout):\n\n```sh\npython -B scripts/verify_frontier799.py --work /tmp/t37-base799\npython -B research/complex-t37-owners/verify.py \\\n  --work /tmp/t37-replay --baseline799 /tmp/t37-base799\npython -B research/complex-t37-owners/package_controls.py \\\n  --out /tmp/t37-package-controls.json\npython -B research/complex-t37-owners/binding_controls.py \\\n  --work /tmp/t37-replay --baseline /tmp/t37-base799 \\\n  --out /tmp/t37-binding-controls.json\n```\n\nOmit `--baseline799` for a single-command cold rebuild. Explicit reuse rechecks complete ancestry coverage and official source/artifact bindings.\n\nThe focused CI runs the default cold rebuild on Ubuntu/Python 3.11 and 3.14, followed by actual-file binding controls, and uploads compact evidence. Hosted CI status is reported separately from local verification.\n",
